  "worked_solution": "First, since $s=4t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{4}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with $s\\ge 0$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{4}) \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}))\\,j \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
